---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import BlockText from '../components/BlockText.astro';
import { dots } from '../lib/patterns.js';
import homeadeReleases from '../data/homeade-releases.json';
import windows from '../data/homeade-windows.json';
import fieldadeReleases from '../data/fieldade-releases.json';
import site from '../data/site.json';
const latest = homeadeReleases[0];
const fieldade = fieldadeReleases[0];
const cardsBg = dots();

// Each card carries a tag for every part of the work it shows,
// and each tag links to the page for that part.
const tag = {
  software: ['/software', 'Custom build'],
  phone: ['/software#phone-apps', 'Phone apps'],
  assistants: ['/knowledge-assistants', 'AI system'],
};
---
<Base title="Products" description="FieldADE and HomeADE keep one folder of plain notes that every agent chat reads, so nothing is explained twice. Plus custom builds: LightScan, Flourish Financial Group, and Kingdom Guide.">
  <Hero variant="graph" seed={5} eyebrow="Products" title="File it once. Every chat reads it.">
    <p class="lede">FieldADE on the phone and HomeADE on the desk share one folder of plain notes. Everything you file under a project is read by every later chat on it, so no agent starts from zero and the folder is worth more each month. Below them, the builds I have shipped for clients and for my own family.</p>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section band-parallax">
    <div class="band-bg" data-parallax="0.3" set:html={cardsBg} aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="wrap">
      <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:wght@700&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@600&display=swap" />
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card work-card" id="fieldade">
          <header class="brand-head bh-ade">
            <img class="app-icon" src="/brand/fieldade-icon.png" alt="" width="56" height="56" />
            <div><h3 class="bh-name"><a href="/fieldade"><BlockText text="FieldADE" /></a></h3></div>
          </header>
          <div class="work-shots">
            <img class="work-shot look-pro-only" src="/work/fieldade.png?v=20261120" alt="FieldADE on an iPhone: a chat with Claude, with a card asking to allow or deny a file edit" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
            <img class="work-shot look-dos-only" src="/work/fieldade-dos.png?v=20261120" alt="FieldADE on an iPhone: a chat with Claude, with a card asking to allow or deny a file edit, in the DOS look" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
            <img class="work-shot look-pro-only" src="/work/fieldade-list.png?v=20261120" alt="FieldADE's Sessions screen: how much of each assistant's limit is used, and the list of open chats" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
            <img class="work-shot look-dos-only" src="/work/fieldade-list-dos.png?v=20261120" alt="FieldADE's Sessions screen: how much of each assistant's limit is used, and the list of open chats, in the DOS look" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p>The phone end of the system. Mail, texts, a photo, or a link arrive, and you file each one under a project with a swipe. That note is now part of the project, and the next chat on it reads it.</p>
          <p>Start a chat from anywhere. It opens with the project note, the rules, and the skills on your computer, so you never type the brief again. You see which model is in use, and you allow each change before it happens.</p>
          <p class="card-actions"><a class="store-badge" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/fieldade/id6828288883" rel="noopener"><img src="/brand/app-store-badge.svg" alt="Download on the App Store" width="132" height="44" /></a> <a class="btn" href="/fieldade">About FieldADE</a> <a class="btn" href="/fieldade/setup">Setup guide</a></p>
          <p class="fine">Version {fieldade.version} &middot; iOS 17+ &middot; <a href="/fieldade#releases">Release notes</a></p>
          <p class="tags">{[tag.phone, tag.software, tag.assistants].map(([href, label]) => <a class="tag" href={href}>{label}</a>)}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card work-card" id="homeade">
          <header class="brand-head bh-ade">
            <img class="app-icon" src="/brand/homeade-icon.png" alt="" width="56" height="56" />
            <div><h3 class="bh-name"><a href="/homeade"><BlockText text="HomeADE" /></a></h3></div>
          </header>
          <div class="work-shots work-shots-wide">
            <img class="work-shot-wide look-pro-only" src="/work/homebase.png?v=20261120" alt="HomeADE on the desktop: a sidebar of screens with each assistant's limit, the list of open chats, and a Claude chat with a card asking to allow or deny a file edit" width="1200" height="814" loading="lazy" />
            <img class="work-shot-wide look-dos-only" src="/work/homebase-dos.png?v=20261120" alt="HomeADE on the desktop in the DOS look: a sidebar of screens with each assistant's limit, the list of open chats, and a Claude chat with a card asking to allow or deny a file edit" width="1200" height="814" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p>The desk on your computer where the notes live. Ingest takes what comes in, proposes where it belongs, and files it as a plain Markdown note in a folder you own. You confirm each one, so nothing is filed unseen.</p>
          <p>Those notes are the agent's memory, a second brain it reads before it answers. Each note you file is context for every later chat on that project, so the agent asks less and does more as the folder grows. Skills, rules, and models sit in one list where you and the agent can find them. FieldADE is optional.</p>
          <p class="card-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=HomeADE%20download`}>Ask for a download</a> <a class="btn" href="/homeade">About HomeADE</a> <a class="btn" href="/homeade/setup">Setup guide</a></p>
          <p class="fine">Mac: version {latest.version} &middot; macOS 14+ &middot; <a href="/homeade#releases">Release notes</a><br />Windows: version {windows.version} beta &middot; Windows 10+ &middot; <a href="/homeade/setup#windows">unsigned</a></p>
          <p class="tags">{[tag.software, tag.assistants].map(([href, label]) => <a class="tag" href={href}>{label}</a>)}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card work-card" id="lightscan">
          <header class="brand-head bh-lightscan">
            <svg class="app-icon" viewBox="0 0 56 56" width="56" height="56" aria-hidden="true">
              <defs><linearGradient id="ls-heat" x1="0" y1="1" x2="1" y2="0"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#2f6bff" /><stop offset=".4" stop-color="#2fd17a" /><stop offset=".7" stop-color="#ffd23f" /><stop offset="1" stop-color="#ff5a3c" /></linearGradient></defs>
              <rect width="56" height="56" rx="13" fill="#11151c" />
              <path d="M12 14h20v10h12v18H12z" fill="url(#ls-heat)" opacity=".9" />
              <path d="M12 14h20v10h12v18H12z" fill="none" stroke="#f3f1ec" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              <path d="M12 23h20M12 33h32M22 14v28M32 24v18" stroke="#11151c" stroke-width="1" opacity=".55" />
              <path d="M6 28h44" stroke="#f3f1ec" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="2 2" />
            </svg>
            <div><h3 class="bh-name"><a href="/lightscan"><span class="ls-light">Light</span>Scan</a></h3></div>
          </header>
          <div class="work-shots">
            <img class="work-shot" src="/software/lightscan.png" alt="LightScan on an iPhone: a scanned house drawn as a floor plan with wall lengths, and a heat map of high and low spots in the floor" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p>An iPhone app for a foundation repair company. The estimator walks the house, and the phone's laser scanner draws the floor plan and a heat map of where the floor sags.</p>
          <p>The app turns the scan into a customer report and a model you can 3D print. The first version was on their phone a day after they described the problem. <a href="/lightscan">About LightScan</a></p>
          <p class="tags">{[tag.phone, tag.software].map(([href, label]) => <a class="tag" href={href}>{label}</a>)}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card work-card" id="flourish">
          <header class="brand-head bh-flourish">
            <svg class="bh-leaf" viewBox="0 0 120 220" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M60 215 C 62 160, 58 110, 66 40" stroke="#0a192f" stroke-width="3" />
              <g stroke="#0a192f" stroke-width="3"><path d="M66 40 C 80 22, 100 18, 112 20 C 108 40, 92 56, 66 40 Z" /><path d="M64 70 C 44 60, 30 44, 28 30 C 46 32, 62 46, 64 70 Z" /><path d="M62 100 C 82 92, 100 96, 110 104 C 96 116, 76 116, 62 100 Z" /></g>
              <g stroke="#00a896" stroke-width="3"><path d="M60 135 C 40 128, 22 112, 18 96 C 38 98, 56 112, 60 135 Z" /><path d="M60 170 C 78 160, 98 162, 110 172 C 96 186, 76 186, 60 170 Z" /><path d="M60 200 C 42 196, 26 184, 22 170 C 40 170, 56 182, 60 200 Z" /></g>
            </svg>
            <div><h3 class="bh-name"><a href="/flourish">Flourish Financial Group</a></h3></div>
          </header>
          <div class="work-shots work-shots-wide">
            <a href="https://flourishfinancialgroup.org"><img class="work-shot-wide" src="/software/flourish.jpg" alt="The Flourish Financial Group home page: a navy banner reading A plan you built, with someone in your corner, a photo of the counselor, and a button to book a free consult" width="1000" height="601" loading="lazy" /></a>
          </div>
          <p>A website for an accredited financial counselor, live about a month after the first conversation. It is static, loads fast, and costs $0 a month to host.</p>
          <p>The site lives in her own GitHub account with a written guide, so she updates it herself and never waits on me. <a href="/flourish">About this site</a></p>
          <p class="tags">{[tag.software].map(([href, label]) => <a class="tag" href={href}>{label}</a>)}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card work-card" id="kingdom-guide">
          <header class="brand-head bh-kingdom">
            <img class="app-icon" src="/brand/kingdom-guide-icon.png" alt="" width="56" height="56" />
            <div><h3 class="bh-name"><a href="/kingdom-guide">Kingdom Guide</a></h3></div>
            <span class="kg-trail" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          </header>
          <div class="work-shots">
            <img class="work-shot" src="/software/kingdom-guide-plan.png" alt="Kingdom Guide's day plan on an iPhone: rides in walking order with arrival times and posted waits, starting with booking TRON as the first Disability Access Service return" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
            <img class="work-shot" src="/software/kingdom-guide-map.png" alt="Kingdom Guide's map: Next is Buzz Lightyear, a notice to book TRON next on the Disability Access Service, and a dashed route through numbered stops labeled with wait times" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p>An iPhone app that plans a day at Magic Kingdom. It puts the rides a family picks in walking order and shows when they will reach each one, with the posted waits.</p>
          <p>For families who use the Disability Access Service, it says which ride to book next. It began as a page for our own trip.</p>
          <p class="card-actions"><a class="store-badge" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/kingdom-guide-park-planner/id6825921966" rel="noopener"><img src="/brand/app-store-badge.svg" alt="Download on the App Store" width="132" height="44" /></a> <a class="btn" href="/kingdom-guide">About Kingdom Guide</a></p>
          <p class="tags">{[tag.phone, tag.software].map(([href, label]) => <a class="tag" href={href}>{label}</a>)}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .work-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; overflow: hidden; }
  .work-card > p:not(.fine):not(.tags):not(.card-actions) { margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
  .work-card .tags { margin-top: auto; padding-top: .5rem; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem; }
  .work-card a.tag { text-decoration: none; }
  .work-card .card-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: .6rem; margin: .5rem 0 .5rem; }
  .work-card .fine { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted, inherit); margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .store-badge { display: inline-flex; line-height: 0; }
  .store-badge img { height: 44px; width: auto; }
  .work-shots { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: .75rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .work-shots-wide { margin: 0 0 1rem; display: block; }
  .work-shot-wide { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .work-shot { display: block; flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; max-width: 200px; height: auto; border-radius: 22px; border: 1px solid var(--line); }

  /* Card headers: each one wears its product's own brand. */
  .brand-head { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .9rem; margin: -1.25rem -1.4rem 1.1rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem; }
  .brand-head .app-icon { flex: none; width: 56px; height: 56px; border-radius: 13px; }
  .work-card .brand-head .bh-name { color: inherit; margin: 0; font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1.15; }
  .work-card .brand-head .bh-name a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .work-card .brand-head .bh-name a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .bh-ade { background: #1c1f26; color: #f3f1ec; }
  .bh-ade .app-icon { box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.12); }
  .bh-ade .bh-name { font-size: 1.4rem; }

  .bh-lightscan { background: #11151c; color: #f3f1ec; font-family: var(--mono); }
  .bh-lightscan::after { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; height: 4px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #2f6bff, #2fd17a 40%, #ffd23f 70%, #ff5a3c); }
  .bh-lightscan .bh-name { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .bh-lightscan .ls-light { font-weight: 400; opacity: .7; }

  .bh-flourish { background: #fff; color: #0a192f; border-bottom: 1px solid #e3e7eb; box-shadow: inset 5px 0 0 #00a896; font-family: "Source Sans 3", var(--sans); }
  .bh-flourish .bh-leaf { flex: none; width: 30px; height: 56px; }
  .bh-flourish .bh-name { font-family: "Cormorant Garamond", Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.6rem; letter-spacing: 0; }

  .bh-kingdom { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #1f9e8a, #0d5546); color: #fff; font-family: ui-rounded, "SF Pro Rounded", var(--sans); }
  .bh-kingdom .app-icon { box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.25); }
  .bh-kingdom .bh-name { font-family: ui-rounded, "SF Pro Rounded", var(--sans); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .kg-trail { position: absolute; right: 1.1rem; top: .8rem; display: flex; gap: .3rem; }
  .kg-trail i { width: .55rem; height: .55rem; border-radius: 50%; border: 1.5px solid #fff; }
  .kg-trail i:nth-child(1) { background: #e8b83a; } .kg-trail i:nth-child(2) { background: #6cc56c; } .kg-trail i:nth-child(3) { background: #e08a4c; }
  .kg-trail i:nth-child(4) { background: #6ea8f0; } .kg-trail i:nth-child(5) { background: #e57cbf; } .kg-trail i:nth-child(6) { background: #a48ef0; }

  /* DOS look: headers go monochrome and mono; the app icons stay. */
  :global(html[data-look="dos"]) .brand-head { background: #000; color: var(--phosphor); font-family: var(--mono); box-shadow: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  :global(html[data-look="dos"]) .brand-head .bh-name { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0; }
  :global(html[data-look="dos"]) .bh-lightscan::after, :global(html[data-look="dos"]) .kg-trail { display: none; }
  :global(html[data-look="dos"]) .bh-flourish .bh-leaf path, :global(html[data-look="dos"]) .bh-lightscan svg path { stroke: var(--phosphor); }
  :global(html[data-look="dos"]) .brand-head .app-icon { border-radius: 0; }
</style>

